<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Convention of Ocaña</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1828">1828</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Convention of Ocaña was a constitutional assembly of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Gran</a> Colombia that met at Ocaña in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a> from April to June 1828 to reform the Constitution of 1821. Bolívar's supporters, who wanted a stronger central government, and the followers of Santander, who favoured limits on executive power, could not agree, and the Bolivarians walked out. Bolívar then assumed dictatorial powers.</p></div>
